    "result": "I haven't changed anything, because the two tests in `test/cart.test.js` contradict each other. No single formula in `total()` can pass both.\n\n- **Existing test (line 19):** it expects tax on the *discounted* amount. For a 3000 subtotal with a 10% discount and 20% tax, that is 3000 − 300 = 2700, plus 540 tax, giving **3240**. This matches the doc comment on `total()` in `src/cart.js`.\n- **Failing test (line 24):** it expects tax on the *full* subtotal. For a 1000 subtotal with a 50% discount and 10% tax, that is 1000 + 100 − 500 = **600**.\n\nIf I switch to tax-before-discount, the line-19 test would give 3000 + 600 − 300 = 3300 instead of 3240, so it would fail. The only way to pass both is to special-case inputs, which would be a hack.\n\nWhich rule is correct?\n\n1. **Tax on the full subtotal (new rule):** I'd change `total()` to `sub + round(sub*taxRate) − round(sub*discount)`, update the doc comment, and fix the line-19 test to expect 3300.\n2. **Tax on the discounted amount (current behaviour):** the code stays as it is, and the line-24 test should expect 550 instead of 600.\n\nTell me which one and I'll make the change and run `npm test`.",
